Current list of drivers to be implemented and the status of re-implementation
=====================================================

bus
 * drvPExpert - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCOHare - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvOHare; see tools/ppc_package_check.py

ide
 * drvPPCSwimFloppy - needs compiled and then tested

input
 * drvPPCSerialPort - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCCuda - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvCuda; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCPMU - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvPMU; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvIOADBDevice - STUB, no in-tree source; class/selector list scaffolded from the
   shipped binary, every method body empty

network
 * drvPPCGem - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCGNic - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCBMac - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvBMacEnet; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCMace - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvMaceEnet; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCDec21040 - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvDECchip21040; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvDEC21x4Ethernet - STUB, no in-tree source; class/selector list scaffolded from the
   shipped binary, every method body empty

scsi
 * drvPPC53c96 - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvApple96_SCSI; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCMesh - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvAppleMesh_SCSI; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCSym8xx - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvSymbios8xx; see tools/ppc_package_check.py

sound
 * drvPPCAwacs - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCBurgundy - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCTASAudio - needs compiled and then tested

video

Nine of the entries above marked "copy of ..." are byte-identical copies of the
sources they cite, which also still live under src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/ and
build into the kernel via conf/files.ppc; the two copies are not kept in sync
automatically. Run tools/ppc_package_check.py to check whether they have
drifted apart.

The two entries marked STUB have no implementation at all: their headers and
.m files declare every selector the shipped binary carries, with empty
method bodies, so a later reconstruction has a starting point.
